; Leg CE -- the host SENDS.  The Victor RECEIVES 32 KB at 38400.
;
; THE NULL LEG for the prefixing fix, and it is the one that says the
; shipping binary did not otherwise move.  Prefixing is a SENDER-side
; decision -- ctlp[] is read only by bgetpkt() and getpkt(), the packet
; BUILDERS (SS16ae) -- so a change to the Victor's prefixing has no
; mechanism by which it can affect a Victor receive.  This leg is here to
; check that claim rather than to assert it.
;
; PASS is SS16ah leg BC/BD's shape:
;
;     rxlost=0  rxfull=0  rxpeak 2,4xx-2,6xx of 4096
;     18 packets, 0 retransmissions, 0 timeouts
;     rxbytes ~37,55x, byte-exact md5
;
; DO NOT read a cps difference against BC or BD.  Those legs are 1.277 s
; apart from each other on one binary (SS16ah, NEXT_SESSION item 5b), so
; anything this leg does inside ~1.3 s is the bench, not the change.  The
; counters are the instrument here; the clock is not.
;
; Reconcile the two ends afterwards, which is a check neither one can do
; alone:
;
;     python3 v9k/tools/pktstat.py --rxbytes <rxbytes from STEPCE.OUT> \
;                                  s16aiCE.pkt
;
; Residual should be -11 (no startup timeout) or +28 (with one).  Anything
; else means the log and the Victor did not see the same transfer.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16aiCE.pkt
send rcvce.dat
statistics
